# Three-Robot Triage
#
# Exactly one of three key stations is active.  The active key unlocks
# its corresponding vault, which has two shelves; XOR forces both
# shelves to be checked to locate the document.
#
# Layout (y-axis: up = North):
#
#    key-a(10,80)   key-b(50,90)   key-c(90,80)
#
#              hub(50,50)
#
#    vA1(5,15) vA2(20,15)    vB1(45,15) vB2(55,15)    vC1(80,15) vC2(95,15)
#    [vault A]               [vault B]                 [vault C]
#
# Routing:
#   key(key-a)=T  →  document in vault A (vA1 or vA2)
#   key(key-b)=T  →  document in vault B (vB1 or vB2)
#   key(key-c)=T  →  document in vault C (vC1 or vC2)
#
# Why 3 robots are required for the optimal plan (time metric):
#   There are 3 possible active keys and 2 robots can only check 2
#   simultaneously.  In the adversarial (minimax) worst case the active
#   key is whichever was NOT checked first.
#
#   With 2 robots: R1→key-a, R2→key-b in parallel.  If both are
#     inactive, one robot must travel on to key-c (extra phase).
#     Worst-case makespan = key travel + key-to-key travel + vault travel.
#
#   With 3 robots: R1→key-a, R2→key-b, R3→key-c all in parallel.
#     Active key is always identified in the FIRST phase.  Two robots
#     then converge on the correct vault (XOR requires both shelves).
#     Worst-case makespan = max(key travel) + max(key-to-vault travel).
#
# With 2 bays and 2 robots, robots can cover every shelf by brute force.
# With 3 vaults the brute-force strategy requires sequentially visiting
# all 6 shelves with 2 robots — always slower than 3-robot parallel
# key checks followed by a single targeted vault visit.

# LOCATIONS
location hub   at 50, 50
location key-a at 10, 80
location key-b at 50, 90
location key-c at 90, 80
location vA1   at  5, 15
location vA2   at 20, 15
location vB1   at 45, 15
location vB2   at 55, 15
location vC1   at 80, 15
location vC2   at 95, 15

# ROBOTS: three start at the central hub
robots 2
robot r1 starts-at hub
robot r2 starts-at hub

# PROPERTIES
recognizable-property key
recognizable-property doc

# GROUND FACTS: key only at the three key stations
!key(hub)
!key(vA1)
!key(vA2)
!key(vB1)
!key(vB2)
!key(vC1)
!key(vC2)

# GROUND FACTS: doc only in vault shelves
!doc(hub)
!doc(key-a)
!doc(key-b)
!doc(key-c)

# WORLD CONSTRAINTS
# Exactly one key is active
{
  key(key-a) | key(key-b) | key(key-c)
}
[?u, ?v | ?u != ?v] {
  key(?u) -> !key(?v)
}

# key-a routes to vault A only
{
  key(key-a) -> (doc(vA1) | doc(vA2))
}
{
  key(key-a) -> (!doc(vB1) & !doc(vB2) & !doc(vC1) & !doc(vC2))
}
# key-b routes to vault B only
{
  key(key-b) -> (doc(vB1) | doc(vB2))
}
{
  key(key-b) -> (!doc(vA1) & !doc(vA2) & !doc(vC1) & !doc(vC2))
}
# key-c routes to vault C only
{
  key(key-c) -> (doc(vC1) | doc(vC2))
}
{
  key(key-c) -> (!doc(vA1) & !doc(vA2) & !doc(vB1) & !doc(vB2))
}

# QUERY: identify active key then verify document shelf via XOR
Query: {
  (key(key-a) & (doc(vA1) ^ doc(vA2))) |
  (key(key-b) & (doc(vB1) ^ doc(vB2))) |
  (key(key-c) & (doc(vC1) ^ doc(vC2)))
}
